<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lower Saxony</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Niedersachsen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> (Niedersachsen) is a state in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>, stretching from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> and the Frisian islands to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harz">Harz</a> mountains. It was formed by the British occupation authorities in 1946 from the Prussian province of Hanover and the states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>, Oldenburg and Schaumburg-Lippe. Many medieval counties and principalities of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> lay within its territory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lower-saxony.jpg" alt="Lower Saxony" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Lower_Saxony.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
